{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"x left parenthesis r minus 9 right parenthesis plus 4 equals 19 x plus 27\"><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given equation, <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> is a positive integer. If the given equation has exactly one solution, what CANNOT be the value of <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["68a009c6-ac1a-43ce-9f86-0fa98b6fac3e"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "f9efc502-a1dc-4d43-8cab-6063152fa431", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "1f21d2ad-fdb7-46ac-b862-aabb36f64b27", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "0575b574-c2e1-4e11-b7cb-bd7b3b18b6af", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "68a009c6-ac1a-43ce-9f86-0fa98b6fac3e", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. In the given equation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x left parenthesis r minus 9 right parenthesis plus 4 equals 19 x plus 27\"><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>27</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is a positive integer. Distributing on the left-hand side of this equation yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r x minus 9 x plus 4 equals 19 x plus 27\"><mi>r</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>27</mn></math>. Subtracting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r x minus 9 x equals 19 x plus 23\"><mi>r</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>23</mn></math>. Subtracting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"19 x\"><mn>19</mn><mi>x</mi></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r x minus 28 x equals 23\"><mi>r</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>28</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn></math>, which can be written as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis r minus 28 right parenthesis x equals 23\"><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn></math>. For this equation to have exactly one solution, the coefficient of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis r minus 28 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, cannot be equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn></math> CANNOT be the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "2a3b6ab6-2f25-4e2a-817b-9112e317c958", "correct_answer": ["D"]}